  "source": "Bronkhorst, Modbus slave interface for digital Mass Flow / Pressure instruments, document 9.17.035 (27-03-2013)",
  "notes": ["Addresses are the PDU addresses of the manual (register number minus 1). The manual lists only the most commonly used parameters.", "RS485 two-wire, RTU (MBC3 and MASS-VIEW can also use ASCII). Delivered with address 1 and 19200 baud; 9600, 19200 and 38400 baud everywhere, 57600 and 115200 on MBC3 only.", "Parity is even and fixed on MBCII, CORI-FLOW and MASS-VIEW; MBC3 allows even, odd or none (no parity needs 2 stop bits).", "Byte parameters read as a 16-bit register with the upper byte 0. Floats and long integers use two registers, high word first; strings hold two characters per register, first character in the high byte.", "Reading a part of a two-register parameter returns exception 02; reading a write-only register returns exception 04.", "A reply takes up to 100 ms. A read response is limited to 100 bytes at 9600 baud, 200 at 19200 and 400 at 38400.", "Meaning of the values (units, control modes, alarm modes) is in the Operation instructions for digital instruments, document 9.17.023."],
